    "updated_at": "2020-07-28T09:37:01Z",
    "body": "My 2 cents: We should keep the v1 focused on XSS. I'd really like the sanitizer to be easy to use for not-security-trained web devs.\r\n\r\nv2: I think it makes a lot of sense to look at sanitizer-adjacent use-cases for a v2, where an application might have app-specific constraints (like conditions on outgoing urls, or styles, or whatnot). If we can provide additional dev value without impairing the main use case we should probably do so, just not in the first step",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
